WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.101 --> 00:00:08.396
Jacob sat with the Christmas present from his grandparents on his lap while the whole family looked on.

2
00:00:08.397 --> 00:00:14.273
"Let me guess," he said, slowly unwrapping the box with a forced smile.

3
00:00:14.274 --> 00:00:20.636
"Socks again?" He opened the box and found a piece of paper instead.

4
00:00:20.637 --> 00:00:23.202
It was a handwritten note that read:

5
00:00:23.203 --> 00:00:30.606
"Merry Christmas! You, Jacob Price, are the owner of five shares of Orange Software Company's stock."

6
00:00:30.607 --> 00:00:35.092
"Instead of socks, we got you stock!" Grandpa said.

7
00:00:35.093 --> 00:00:38.660
"Thank you, Grandpa and Grandma!" Jacob said.

8
00:00:38.661 --> 00:00:44.157
"I love Orange's games! Does this mean I'm going to be rich?"

9
00:00:44.158 --> 00:00:50.068
Everyone laughed.

10
00:00:50.069 --> 00:00:52.844
"Come with me," Grandpa said.

11
00:00:52.845 --> 00:01:02.170
He led Jacob into his office as the rest of the family opened their last presents.

12
00:01:02.171 --> 00:01:06.938
"Your grandmother and I wanted to give you something different this year.

13
00:01:06.939 --> 00:01:11.194
Your parents told us not to give you money since you'd just spend it."

14
00:01:11.195 --> 00:01:17.468
Jacob grinned sheepishly. "What else can you do with money besides save or spend it?"

15
00:01:17.469 --> 00:01:20.936
"You can invest it," Grandpa said.

16
00:01:20.937 --> 00:01:25.923
"Your present this year is an introduction to investing in the stock market."

17
00:01:25.924 --> 00:01:28.976
Jacob looked down at the note again.

18
00:01:28.977 --> 00:01:33.183
"I'm an owner—but I don't own the whole company, right?"

19
00:01:33.184 --> 00:01:38.815
Grandpa smiled. "Right. You own stock in the company.

20
00:01:38.816 --> 00:01:41.524
Stock is ownership in the company.

21
00:01:41.525 --> 00:01:44.000
You own five shares.

22
00:01:44.001 --> 00:01:46.615
A share is a unit of ownership.

23
00:01:46.616 --> 00:01:51.496
Companies sell stock to raise money."

24
00:01:51.497 --> 00:01:55.603
"Don't they make enough money with their products?" Jacob asked.

25
00:01:55.604 --> 00:02:01.687
"Orange Software has a new game coming out soon—it's going to sell millions of copies!"

26
00:02:01.688 --> 00:02:08.799
"Orange makes a lot of money, but companies always need more money to help them expand or compete with other companies.

27
00:02:08.800 --> 00:02:14.975
They can use the money from selling stock to develop new products or improve existing ones.

28
00:02:14.976 --> 00:02:20.897
They can also use the money to hire employees or cover other business costs."

29
00:02:20.898 --> 00:02:25.707
Jacob nodded. "Now I get why companies sell stock.

30
00:02:25.708 --> 00:02:28.559
But how do people make money buying it?"

31
00:02:28.560 --> 00:02:33.932
"It's an investment—using money to make more money," Grandpa said.

32
00:02:33.933 --> 00:02:39.804
"If a company does well, and its profits go up, stock owners share in the profits.

33
00:02:39.805 --> 00:02:44.052
Then they can sell their stock at a higher price than they first paid."

34
00:02:44.053 --> 00:02:50.021
"Cool," Jacob said. "Money that grows!"

35
00:02:50.022 --> 00:02:54.120
"It can also go the other way," Grandpa warned.

36
00:02:54.121 --> 00:03:01.005
"Investing is often risky. If the company loses money, the stock price goes down.

37
00:03:01.006 --> 00:03:07.336
There's no guarantee which way it will go."

38
00:03:07.337 --> 00:03:14.017
Jacob didn't think much about his present until one morning a few weeks later.

39
00:03:14.018 --> 00:03:21.472
"Orange's latest game has already sold thousands of copies since its release," Dad said from behind a newspaper.

40
00:03:21.473 --> 00:03:24.686
"The stock price increased 7 percent."

41
00:03:24.687 --> 00:03:27.754
"Does that mean I'm making money?"

42
00:03:27.755 --> 00:03:38.376
"Yep." Dad showed Jacob the stock market section of the paper, pointing to Orange Software's listing.

43
00:03:38.377 --> 00:03:45.807
"Whoa!" Jacob said. "I made $17.50!"

44
00:03:45.808 --> 00:03:53.420
Soon Jacob began paying more attention to the stock market, checking Orange Software's stock every day.

45
00:03:53.421 --> 00:03:58.338
Some days it increased a little, while other days it increased a lot.

46
00:03:58.339 --> 00:04:02.052
Then there were days when the stock price dropped a little.

47
00:04:02.053 --> 00:04:08.798
And one day, after a serious glitch was discovered in a game, the price dropped a lot.

48
00:04:08.799 --> 00:04:12.581
When Grandpa called, Jacob talked to him about it.

49
00:04:12.582 --> 00:04:17.174
"Don't worry too much about little ups or downs," Grandpa said.

50
00:04:17.175 --> 00:04:20.625
"It's better to think in the long term with investing.

51
00:04:20.626 --> 00:04:24.166
Stock prices go up and down every day.

52
00:04:24.167 --> 00:04:29.076
Focus on whether a stock does well or not over a longer period of time."

53
00:04:29.077 --> 00:04:33.624
For the next year, Jacob tracked Orange's stock.

54
00:04:33.625 --> 00:04:37.812
By the following Christmas, it had doubled in price.

55
00:04:37.813 --> 00:04:42.177
Jacob had also been working on saving a lot of his allowance.

56
00:04:42.178 --> 00:04:47.673
"I'm thinking about buying more stock someday," he said to Grandpa.

57
00:04:47.674 --> 00:04:52.991
"I did lots of research before buying stock in Orange," Grandpa said.

58
00:04:52.992 --> 00:04:56.871
"Big or popular companies aren't always a wise choice.

59
00:04:56.872 --> 00:05:01.540
It's important to read about a company in order to make a smart investment."

60
00:05:01.541 --> 00:05:03.989
"Got it," Jacob said.

61
00:05:03.990 --> 00:05:11.325
After dinner, when it was time to open presents, Jacob reached for Grandpa and Grandma's package first.

62
00:05:11.326 --> 00:05:15.797
"More stock?" he asked, eagerly tearing into the present.

63
00:05:15.798 --> 00:05:24.372
"Since you've already learned about the stock market and investing . . . " Grandpa grinned. "We went back to—"

64
00:05:24.373 --> 00:05:31.907
Jacob laughed. "Socks!"

